h his new line of work  making himself a special fire resistant  suit and an array of new weapons before  taking on the guise of the supervillain  Firefly according to we got this  coverage report an early production  document indicates that lanes backstory  will possibly be revised to make him a  man in his 20s who grew up orphaned  before embarking on a fiery rampage  against the privileged people of Gotham  which could make for an interesting  parallel with Batman's own backstory  the Mad Hatter's history stretches even  further back in DC Laura all the way to  his first appearance in 1948 Batman  number 49 first portrayed is a common  criminal with an unusual affinity for  his namesake  Jervis Tetch has since been shown to  possess a high degree of skill and  electrical engineering which he uses to  produce his signature devices  mind-controlling hats as for the other  bad guys said to be on tap for the  Batman any of them could be solid  choices just so long as they're done  properly the penguin and the Riddler are  two iconic villains whose previous big  screen appearances tended toward the  garish and comedic and while two-face  was certainly done justice by Aaron  Eckhart's performance in The Dark Knight  many fans felt that the character was  given too little screen time as for  Catwoman well whoever ends up taking  that role has some mighty boots to fill  however it all shakes out it's important  to remember that none of this is  confirmed and those characters could  easily be swapped out or cut all  together before the Batman's final  shooting script is in place after all  front-loading a film with six villains  seems mighty ambitious and it's not like  superhero movies haven't struggled to  juggle bad guys in the past I know all  these guys come from whatever course  Reeves does choose to take fans will  just have to have faith in his talent  and hope that the director can deliver  both the Batman we need and the Batman  we deserve check out one of our n